---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About QSO Forge"
  description="QSO Forge builds engineering-quality amateur radio software. Cross-platform from day one. Offline-first because the field doesn't have a hotspot."
  path="/about"
  ogImage="/og/about.png"
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Software the field can rely on."
    subtitle="QSO Forge builds amateur radio software for operators who care about how their tools behave. Cross-platform from day one. Offline-first because the field doesn't have a hotspot. Built in the open enough to earn trust, closed enough to fund the work."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
    <h2 class="mb-6 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-text-muted">
      Principles
    </h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <article
        class="rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-surface-1)] p-5"
      >
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">
          Engineering quality first
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          The shipped app is the spec. We write things down, we test what we
          build, and we sweat the workflows that operators actually use under
          contest pressure.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-surface-1)] p-5"
      >
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">
          Cross-platform parity
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          Windows and Linux ship together on day one. macOS lands when it
          earns its place. Whatever surface you use, the same data, the same
          keybindings, the same answers.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-surface-1)] p-5"
      >
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">Offline-first</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          DXpeditions, POTA in a canyon, contest stations in remote cabins —
          if it needs a hotspot to work, it's not built for hams. The license,
          the logbook, the rig control: all local.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-surface-1)] p-5"
      >
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-text">Built by hams</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          We're operators. We use what we ship. If a feature feels wrong on
          the air, it doesn't make it into the next release.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
    <h2 class="mb-6 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-text-muted">
      Founder
    </h2>
    <div
      class="rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-surface-1)] p-6"
    >
      <p class="text-text-muted">
        Founder bio placeholder — replace before launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
